<%# The page tree's column as this browser left it (`admin--shell--tree-width`
    remembers the chosen width and the fold in `localStorage`), said on <html>
    before anything is painted: the shell's grid reads `--admin-tree-width`
    (content-spiel.tailwind.css, 17rem without it), so the page is laid out at
    the chosen width from the first paint and the editor does not change width
    when the script connects. A value that is no number, or outside the two
    limits, is nobody's choice and sets nothing.

    THE UNIT IS THE STYLESHEET'S. The divider's figures
    (`Admin::Shell::TreeDividerComponent`) are pixels at a root font size of
    16px, and the stylesheet lays them out in rem, so each limit is multiplied
    here by the root's computed font size over 16, exactly as the controller
    does (its `scale`). That is why this script is rendered AFTER the
    stylesheet's link and not before it as the theme's is: a script waits for
    the stylesheets linked before it, so the font size it reads is the one the
    page is laid out with, whoever sets it (today nobody does: it is the
    browser's own). Still before <body> exists, so still before the first
    paint.

    THE FOLD. `data-tree-folded` says the person folded the column to its
    strip (`FOLD_KEY` holds "1"; `admin--shell--tree-width#fold`). It is set
    here before the first paint, so a folded tree is laid out as the strip
    from the start; the stylesheet asks it from 1024px only, where the tree
    is a column. The chosen width is applied either way: the fold keeps it,
    and an unfold finds it on <html>.

    Both stay on <html> for the life of the document: Turbo replaces <body>
    and merges <head>, never the root element, so a visit and Back find them
    as they were. Guarded like the theme's (`shared/_theme_head`):
    `localStorage` can throw, and the page is then laid out at the default. %>
<% divider = Admin::Shell::TreeDividerComponent %>
<%= javascript_tag nonce: true do %>
  (function () {
    var root = document.documentElement;
    var size = parseFloat(window.getComputedStyle(root).fontSize);
    var scale = size > 0 ? size / <%= divider::BASE %> : 1;
    var stored = NaN;
    var folded = false;
    try { stored = parseFloat(localStorage.getItem("<%= divider::STORAGE_KEY %>")); } catch (e) {}
    try { folded = localStorage.getItem("<%= divider::FOLD_KEY %>") === "1"; } catch (e) {}
    if (stored >= <%= divider::MIN %> * scale && stored <= <%= divider::MAX %> * scale) root.style.setProperty("--admin-tree-width", stored + "px");
    if (folded) root.setAttribute("data-tree-folded", "");
  })();
<% end %>
